    "cross_source_insight": "Drawing from interviews with Andrew Cohen and Bruno Poet combined with the AuraLuxMuse study reveals a consistent theme: whether hand-designed or AI-assisted, lighting and scenic design fundamentally depend on deeply understanding the narrative, space, and audience focus. AI tools accelerate technical workflows but do not replace the core human insight needed to interpret story and context meaningfully.",
    "limitation_note": "The evidence mainly draws from specific theatre productions and controlled AI system evaluations without broad field deployment, so findings may not fully generalize across all theatre genres or scale. Furthermore, some interviews lack fully verified transcripts, which could limit interpretive accuracy."
